{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1776865785,"nonce":"lHXR16KNBpeD1CIBReTsOM6JAQ0=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABABs5eg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/76#issuecomment-4296751482"},"message":"Peer issue for physical install, offset measurements, URDF updates, and SVG diagram: #77","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1777065137,"nonce":"S14J5dkcKFMYl238AanVq4hL7Uk=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAUeiww","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/76#issuecomment-4316439235"},"message":"Unit is confirmed (per `bizzyboat_project11/docs/hydro_payload_install_log.md`) as:\n\n- **SBG Ellipse-D-G4A2-B1** (dual-antenna INS), SN 000034256\n- Serial to mercat **COM4 @ 115200 baud**\n\nSo the TCP-driver and embedded-web-server notes from upstream QPS docs don't apply — the Ellipse-D is configured via **sbgCenter** (close it before starting QINSy — it holds the unit) and feeds QINSy over serial.\n\n## QINSy driver\n\nUse the serial binary driver family:\n\n- **`SBG Systems (R-P-H) – 03`** — position, velocity, heading, pitch/roll/heave, status. This is the main workhorse.\n- **`SBG Systems Vel, Acc, Rot (UTC) – 42`** — optional, add only if we decide to feed raw IMU into QINSy too.\n- **Do NOT** use the TCP variants (`18`) as a time-sync source — QPS explicitly warns jitter is too high to recover UTC cleanly. We're on serial anyway.\n\n## SBG messages to enable on COM4\n\nConfigure in sbgCenter → Output → COM port → Logs. All five \"required\" rows **must** be on — QINSy won't run the template without them.\n\n### Required\n\n| SBG log | QINSy role | Rate |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SBG_ECOM_LOG_STATUS` | Health bits that gate quality of every other message | 1 Hz (or \"new data\") |\n| `SBG_ECOM_LOG_UTC_TIME` | Time-tag of every subsequent frame | \"new data\" (per QPS) |\n| `SBG_ECOM_LOG_EKF_NAV` | Position (lat/lon/alt) + NED velocity; status from `POSITION_VALID` bit in STATUS | 50 Hz |\n| `SBG_ECOM_LOG_EKF_EULER` | Roll, pitch, yaw + per-axis accuracies | 50 Hz |\n| `SBG_ECOM_LOG_SHIP_MOTION` | **Heave** (+ surge, sway, accels) — heave is here, NOT in EKF_EULER | 50 Hz |\n\n### Recommended (dual-antenna)\n\n| SBG log | Why | Rate |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SBG_ECOM_LOG_GPS1_POS` | Raw GNSS PVT — backup / QC of EKF position | GNSS native (5–10 Hz) |\n| `SBG_ECOM_LOG_GPS1_VEL` | Raw GNSS velocity — backup / QC | GNSS native |\n| `SBG_ECOM_LOG_GPS1_HDT` | Raw dual-antenna heading, independent of EKF_EULER yaw — useful for heading cross-check and patch-test diagnostics | GNSS native |\n\n### Optional / diagnostic\n\n- `SBG_ECOM_LOG_IMU_DATA` (or `_IMU_SHORT`) — only needed if we add the `Vel, Acc, Rot (UTC) – 42` driver.\n- `SBG_ECOM_LOG_GPS1_RAW` — raw GNSS observables for Qinertia PPK post-processing. Skip unless we plan to PPK.\n\n## Baud budget on COM4 @ 115200\n\n115200 baud ≈ 11.5 kB/s usable. The required set at 50 Hz + GPS logs at 10 Hz lands around 8–9 kB/s — fine. Adding `IMU_DATA` at 50 Hz pushes to ~11 kB/s and starts dropping frames. If we want raw IMU, drop it to 25 Hz, disable `GPS1_RAW`, or bump COM4 to 230400 / 460800 (confirm the mercat USB-serial driver supports it first).\n\n## QINSy template layout\n\nSame pattern as the Applanix POS MV how-to — one driver instance per role:\n\n1. **Position Navigation System** → position slot (from `EKF_NAV`), reference at Vessel CoG.\n2. **Gyro Compass System** → heading slot (from `EKF_EULER` yaw, or `GPS1_HDT` if preferred).\n3. **Pitch-Roll-Heave Sensor** → motion slot, \"Positive downwards\" (matches SBG FRD convention).\n4. Optional **Miscellaneous-Status** for health decoding.\n5. Time Sync: skip if the M3 and other sensors are already UTC-tagged off GNSS PPS — but note this depends on the NTP/time-sync decision still open on this issue.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- **Heave lives in `SHIP_MOTION`**, not `EKF_EULER`. Enabling only EKF_EULER gives you attitude with no heave, and QINSy silently runs without vertical motion correction.\n- **sbgCenter output is per-interface.** Enabling a log on the USB port does *not* put it on COM4 — each serial port has its own assignment table. Verify the serial-port tab specifically after any config change.\n- **Lever arms in one place only.** Lever arms and IMU-to-vessel alignment are already configured on the SBG side per the install log (IMU at (-0.577, 0, -0.029) m; ANT1 aft, ANT2 fwd). QINSy should reference **Vessel CoG** — do not re-enter lever arms in QINSy or they'll be applied twice.\n- **UTC_TIME validity** depends on a GNSS time fix — until the unit has 3D/RTK fix, the time field is flagged invalid and QINSy may stall on time-sync.\n\n## References\n\n- [SBG Systems (R-P-H) – 03 driver (QPS)](https://confluence.qps.nl/dm/sbg-systems-r-p-h-03-38703231.html)\n- [SBG Systems Vel, Acc, Rot (UTC) – 42 driver (QPS)](https://confluence.qps.nl/dm/sbg-systems-vel-acc-rot-utc-42-38703288.html)\n- [How-to Applanix POS MV – Setup with Qinsy (template pattern)](https://confluence.qps.nl/qinsy/latest/how-to-applanix-pos-mv-setup-with-qinsy-256672342.html)\n- [sbg_ros2_driver (log-name reference)](https://github.com/SBG-Systems/sbg_ros2_driver)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1777069500,"nonce":"/j8aGOvqd7wJietGubt6hPk57S4=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAUyfng","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/76#issuecomment-4316766110"},"message":"Digging into the **1PPS connection** specifically — important update on the time-source plan from my earlier comment.\n\n## Headline: TM2000B can't directly drive the M3's 1PPS\n\nThe TM2000B has **no physical PPS output** — only NTP/PTP over ethernet. Per the TimeMachines manual, the BNC PPS output is a TM2500B/C feature, not TM2000B. So my prior \"TM2000B is the natural 1PPS+ZDA source\" line was wrong; without a TM2500-series swap or a dedicated PPS card we can't use it.\n\nThe natural source on the boat is the **SBG Ellipse-D**.\n\n## Per-device 1PPS details\n\n### M3 (consumer)\n\nFrom `m3_sonar_ins_en_us.pdf` §Synchronization \u0026 §Cable layout:\n\n| Item | Spec |\n|---|---|\n| Electrical | **0 to 5 VDC pulse, 50% duty cycle** |\n| Trigger edge | **Rising** (counters zero on rising edge) |\n| Firmware required | **≥ 1.5** |\n| Companion data | NMEA **ZDA over UDP 31100 @ 1 Hz** to the *sonar head* IP, not the M3 software |\n\nTwo physical input paths:\n\n- **Path A — main 10-pin SEA CON MINK-10-CCPL underwater cable**: pin 3 = 1PPS (white/blue), pin 6 = 1PPS GND. Re-terminating the wet-end on a through-hull install is impractical, so skip this.\n- **Path B — 4-pin auxiliary Sync/1PPS cable into the breakout box** (cable C9 in the interconnect chart): MIND-4-CCP pinout — Pin 1 DGND, Pin 2 PRI_SYNC, Pin 3 DRAIN/shield, **Pin 4 1PPS_SYNC**.\n\n\u003e [!important]\n\u003e The manual lists two breakout box variants: with and without the 4-pin sync/1PPS connector. **We need to confirm ours has it** — if not, we need the sync-capable variant before the class.\n\n### SBG Ellipse-D (producer)\n\nPer SBG Ellipse Boxed electrical specs:\n\n| Item | Spec |\n|---|---|\n| Output pin | **SYNC OUT A — main connector pin 6** |\n| Electrical | LVTTL: high 3.2 V (light load) / 2.6 V @ 16 mA; low 0.1 V / 0.4 V @ 16 mA |\n| Headroom into M3 | M3 wants 0–5 V logic; 3.2 V high is well above standard Vih (~2 V), should latch cleanly. Scope before trusting. |\n| ZDA emission | Configurable in sbgCenter on any UART output — pulse width and PPS mode set per Sync Out config page |\n\n### TM2000B\n\nNo PPS connector. Can emit NMEA ZDA over UDP — useful as a redundant ZDA path but useless for the electrical pulse. Not a viable M3 time source on its own.\n\n### Cube FCU\n\nTheoretical PPS available on C-RTK 2HP, but tapping it couples autonomy and survey chains. Skip.\n\n## Recommended wiring\n\n```\nSBG Ellipse-D\n  Sync Out A (pin 6)  ── LVTTL 1PPS ─→ M3 breakout, 4-pin Sync/1PPS, pin 4 (1PPS_SYNC)\n  GND / shield        ──────────────→ M3 breakout, 4-pin Sync/1PPS, pin 1 (DGND) + pin 3 (DRAIN)\n\n  COM4 NMEA ZDA  ─→ mercat ─→ UDP forwarder ─→ M3 head IP : port 31100  (ZDA @1 Hz)\n```\n\n## Open prerequisites for next pier session\n\n- [ ] **Confirm M3 breakout box variant** has the 4-pin Sync/1PPS connector (photo settles it)\n- [ ] **Confirm M3 head firmware ≥ 1.5** before relying on 1PPS time sync mode\n- [ ] **Decide ZDA bridge mechanism**: QINSy pass-through (cleanest if supported), small Python/PowerShell forwarder on mercat, or other. Ellipse-D is serial-only — no native UDP ZDA from the SBG side.\n- [ ] **Fabricate PPS cable**: SEA CON MIND-4 on the breakout end, SBG main-connector tap on the other; shielded twisted pair, \u003c 1 m. Scope-verify pulse level reaches M3 cleanly.\n- [ ] **Set SBG Sync Out A to PPS mode** in sbgCenter (Output → Sync Out → Pulse mode); record the configured pulse width\n- [ ] **Bench-test 1PPS lock** before water deployment: M3 log should show \"INF 1PPS: 10 pulses received in 10s\"\n\nThese will be added to the `hydro_payload_install_log.md` next-pier-session checklist on the `feature/issue-57` branch.\n\nSources:\n- Local: `~/m3_sonar/m3_sonar_ins_en_us.pdf` §Synchronization, §Cable layout and interconnections\n- [SBG Ellipse Boxed — Electrical Specifications](https://support.sbg-systems.com/sc/el/latest/ellipse-documentation/hardware-documentation/ellipse-boxed-mechanical-electrical-specs/ellipse-boxed-electrical-specifications)\n- [TimeMachines TM2000B Manual (PDF)](https://timemachinescorp.com/wp-content/uploads/TM2000BManual.pdf)\n- [TimeMachines TM2500C Manual — PPS-capable sibling](https://www.manualslib.com/manual/3055388/Time-Machines-Tm2500c.html)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1777073124,"nonce":"f1d4a9kuWWxGJLVnLpFEsDOVQ4g=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAVAqJQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/76#issuecomment-4316998181"},"message":"**Update / supersede the open prerequisites from the previous 1PPS comment.** Three facts confirmed in dialog:\n\n1. **Breakout box variant**: ours is the non-triangular sync-capable variant — has the 4-pin Sync/1PPS connector. The \"confirm breakout box variant\" prerequisite is closed.\n2. **QINSy can emit ZDA over UDP**: it has a `Network NMEA ZDA (UDP) - 18` output driver. `Settings → Input/Output Ports → Output Select = NMEA → enable $--ZDA at 1 Hz`, point at the M3 head IP:31100. So the M3 stays on its isolated mercat link and **mercat sources ZDA via QINSy** — no script needed, no need to renegotiate the M3's network address.\n3. **SBG PORT E can carry RTCM in addition to NMEA out**: in sbgCenter Input/Output tab, set PORT E mode = RS-232 and toggle \"Forward Corrections\". So one full-duplex RS-232 link to gabby does both NMEA out and RTCM in. PORT B (DB-9 #2 pin 8) stays unused.\n\n## Updated wiring picture\n\n```\nSBG splitter DB-9 #2 (SYNC/PORT E, male DTE)\n  ├ pin 4 (SYNC OUT A, LVTTL)  ──┐\n  ├ pin 5 (GND)                  ├─→  M3 breakout 4-pin Sync/1PPS\n  │                              │     (pin 4 = 1PPS_SYNC, pin 1 = DGND, pin 3 = DRAIN)\n  │\n  ├ pin 2 (PORT E RX) ──┐\n  ├ pin 3 (PORT E TX)   ├─→  gabby rear-panel RS-232 (DB-9, male DTE)\n  └ pin 5 (GND, shared) ┘     (full-duplex: NMEA out + RTCM in via \"Forward Corrections\")\n\nQINSy on mercat\n  Network NMEA ZDA (UDP) output ──→ M3 head IP : 31100\n  (over the existing isolated mercat ↔ M3 ethernet link)\n```\n\n## Cable fab spec\n\nSingle fan-out cable from the SBG splitter's DB-9 #2:\n- **SBG end**: female DB-9 (mates with male DTE on the splitter)\n- **gabby end**: female DB-9 (mates with male DTE on gabby's rear panel — gabby is a Neousys Nuvo-9160GC with a MezIO add-in giving 4 native RS-232 ports, all free)\n- **DB-9 ↔ DB-9 wiring**: null-modem (pin 2 ↔ pin 3, pin 3 ↔ pin 2, pin 5 ↔ pin 5) — both ends are DTE\n- **M3 end**: SEA CON MIND-4 plug; gender depends on breakout variant (CCP cable plug = male contacts; FCR cable receptacle = female contacts) — confirm by inspection before ordering the connector\n- 1PPS leg \u003c 1 m; gabby leg can be longer (RS-232 good to ~15 m), shielded twisted pair\n\nPORT A on COM4 to mercat is unchanged; sbgCenter and QINSy on mercat continue to share that link via the established close-sbgCenter-before-QINSy dance.\n\n## Open prerequisites\n\n- [ ] Identify which MIND-4 variant the M3 breakout takes (CCP vs FCR)\n- [ ] M3 head firmware ≥ 1.5\n- [ ] sbgCenter: enable PORT E (RS-232, NMEA out, Forward Corrections) and Sync Out A pulse mode (record pulse width)\n- [ ] Fabricate the cable per the spec above\n- [ ] Configure QINSy `Network NMEA ZDA (UDP) - 18` driver to M3 head IP:31100\n- [ ] Configure gabby NTRIP client to forward RTCM out the chosen MezIO RS-232 port; decide MACORS mountpoint\n- [ ] Verify 1PPS lock at the M3 (`INF 1PPS: 10 pulses received in 10s`) and RTK fixed status in sbgCenter\n\nUpdates committed to `feature/issue-57` in `bizzyboat_project11/docs/hydro_payload_install_log.md`.\n\nSources:\n- [QINSy `Network NMEA ZDA (UDP) - 18` driver](https://confluence.qps.nl/dm/network-nmea-zda-udp-18-3768323.html)\n- [SBG Configure RTK / RTCM port settings](https://support.sbg-systems.com/sc/el/latest/how-to-articles/configure-rtk)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1777076986,"nonce":"VqgkllKbvXBc+oASlAvbdPBpBr4=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAVNnCA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/76#issuecomment-4317210376"},"message":"**Proposed AML SVS architecture: move it to gabby and let gabby be the SV data hub.**\n\nMove the AML serial cable from mercat COM3 to one of gabby's free MezIO RS-232 ports. gabby publishes a ROS topic, sends the raw `$AML…*\u003ccs\u003e` line to mercat as UDP for QINSy, and emits a **Valeport-format** copy out a second MezIO port that connects to mercat (now-free COM3) via a null-modem cable for the M3.\n\n```\nAML SVS ──serial──► gabby (MezIO RS-232 #1)\n                     │\n                     ├── sv_bridge ROS 2 node ──┐\n                     │   ├─► /sound_speed (ROS topic)\n                     │   ├─► UDP datagram → mercat:port (raw $AML line)\n                     │   └─► Valeport string → MezIO RS-232 #2\n                     │\n                     └── null-modem cable to mercat free COM3 → M3 software\n                                                                (Sensors Setup,\n                                                                 native Valeport\n                                                                 SVS protocol)\n\nQINSy on mercat\n  Network - Depth SV Temp (AML or EM1000) - 34   ← UDP from gabby\n                                                   (auto-detects format)\n```\n\n## Why\n\n- **M3 gets native Valeport protocol** — no custom sensor definition needed. The Valeport \"standard\" output is dead simple: leading space + 7-digit mm/s integer + CR/LF (e.g. `_1510123\\r\\n` for 1510.123 m/s).\n- **SV becomes a first-class ROS signal** — logging, operator UI, future autonomy.\n- **gabby as consistent data hub** — pairs with the SBG↔gabby PORT E plan; mercat owns sonar acquisition, gabby owns serial fan-out.\n- **Future AML winch SVP plugs in** without architectural change.\n- **Single AML consumer** — no Y-cable, no virtual COM, no com0com on Windows.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\n- **New failure mode**: M3 and QINSy now depend on gabby's bridge service running. Mitigations: `systemd Restart=always`; configure a sane M3 `Sound Speed Preference` default (~1490 m/s) so M3 isn't dead-on-arrival if the bridge is late on boot.\n- **Cable reroute**: AML cable moves from mercat COM3 to gabby MezIO. Both machines are in the same enclosure, so this is a few feet of shuffling.\n- **Software hop = bug surface**: a buggy bridge poisons both consumers simultaneously. Y-cable is passive and never wrong. Mitigation: keep the bridge tiny, validate raw-vs-emitted continuously.\n\n## Open prerequisites\n\n- Capture 5 lines of the live AML stream from TeraTerm — pins down the exact field layout for the bridge code (and identifies the AML model).\n- Bench-test M3 boot tolerance for late SV (start M3 software with no stream, then start stream — does it pick up cleanly or need restart?).\n- Decide ROS message convention with `marine_tools#1` so both `/sound_speed` publishers agree on the type.\n- Decide bridge package home: extend `marine_tools` or new `aml_sv_bridge` package.\n- Source / fabricate the null-modem cable (off-the-shelf, female DB-9 both ends, pin 2/3 cross).\n\n## Fallback if rejected\n\nAML stays on mercat COM3, QINSy uses the serial `Sound Velocity - Smart SV (AML, ASCII) (Active) - 31` driver, M3 either gets a Y-cable + custom sensor definition or relies on a fixed `Sound Speed Preference` default.\n\nFull architecture and checklist committed to `feature/issue-57` in `bizzyboat_project11/docs/hydro_payload_install_log.md`.\n\nSources:\n- [Valeport miniSVS Operating Manual — output format](https://www.valeport.co.uk/content/uploads/2022/09/miniSVS-Operating-Manual.pdf)\n- [QINSy `Network - Depth SV Temp (AML or EM1000) - 34`](https://confluence.qps.nl/dm/depth-sv-temp-aml-or-em1000-34-25362543.html)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1777086893,"nonce":"oDDM4gXL/SnuGK4iLVKgcDnaPR4=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAVvDmA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/76#issuecomment-4317758360"},"message":"**Survey-readiness round-up beyond the wiring/config thread.** A 10-item check on what's still open between \"M3 cabled and configured\" and \"students walk up at the start of the June class.\" Earlier comments on this issue cover the wiring/config side (SBG, M3, 1PPS, gabby PORT E, AML SVS via gabby). This rolls up the operational-readiness items that emerged from review.\n\nResolved with no further work / matches existing practice:\n\n- **Tide / vertical datum** — ERS for QINSy (no plumbing); ROS-side tide pipeline already tracked separately (`#7/PR#9`, `#20/PR#55`).\n- **Storage** — existing mercat → salmon → UNH-server workflow.\n- **Backup laptop** — accept the risk; matches last year.\n- **Trimble phase-center offsets** — pier task added in commit [`e3d2028`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/commit/e3d2028); photograph the case label, look up phase center.\n- **Network endpoints** — mercat `192.168.20.8` (boat LAN), `192.168.1.8` (M3-isolated NIC), M3 head `192.168.1.234` recorded in install log Hardware Inventory.\n- **Windows Firewall on mercat** — confirmed off; recurring post-Windows-update verification added.\n\nOpen survey-readiness items now captured on `feature/issue-57` in `bizzyboat_project11/docs/hydro_payload_install_log.md` (commit [`6d654e8`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/commit/6d654e8)):\n\n1. **AML-3 SVP via SmartCast winch.** SmartCast = Seafloor winch on the boat; AML-3 = profiler. Workflow mirrors last year's blaze pattern on IzzyBoat (cast → WiFi download → SailFish/SSM → profile file → QINSy). Open prereqs: verify mercat WiFi hardware (USB dongle as fallback), bench-test the winch + AML-3 pipeline end-to-end, confirm QINSy SVP ingestion path.\n\n2. **Patch-test prep.** Students design and run the patch test (cod rock as the feature) — pedagogically intentional. Our prep is just to make sure all measured install offsets (M3, SBG IMU, Trimble antennas, SVS) are committed in the QINSy template and SBG sbgCenter config **before** students walk up. If offsets are unapplied, students chase phantom misalignments that are really just unconverted measurements.\n\n3. **`marine_tools#1` (QINSy → ROS bridge) — critical path for June.** Architecture is sonar-agnostic: QINSy emits processed soundings + TPU via its `Network - Generic Output (User-defined ASCII) (UDP) - 15` driver; ROS 2 node on gabby parses → `PointCloud2` with TPU → existing `cube_bathymetry_node` → `grid_map` → CAMP coverage / rviz. **Supersedes** the per-sonar `.all` parser plan from `project_kongsberg_m3.md` memory. Bonus: TPU comes for free from QINSy's real-time uncertainty chain. BizzyBoat-side prereqs (Generic Layout XML, vertical-reference choice, TPU confidence-level conversion, end-to-end smoke test) added to the install log; ROS-side implementation tracked in [`marine_tools#1`](https://github.com/rolker/marine_tools/issues/1).\n\n4. **M3 mode/range/ping-rate baseline.** Students choose their own settings (matches last year's Norbit pedagogy). Our prep: ensure operator-account access to M3 software, save a known-good config as a class-baseline restore point, mirror the M3 ref manual into the operator-docs area.\n\n## Critical-path summary for June\n\n`marine_tools#1` is the standout. Live CAMP coverage during student-led survey planning depends on it. Wiring/config from the rest of this issue *enables* the soundings; `marine_tools#1` is what turns them into the planning feedback loop students use.\n\nMemory captured at `~/.claude/projects/-home-roland-project11/memory/project_bizzyboat_sonar_architecture.md` for future-session context, with `project_kongsberg_m3.md` updated to flag the Stream-2 supersession.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1777467463,"nonce":"BT/Y9BRcR03J//XaQ9BdnpXoF4U=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAuoGXA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/76#issuecomment-4343858780"},"message":"## Update — COM4 root cause + permanent prevention (2026-04-29)\n\nThe recurring \"SBG COM4 locked after reboot\" issue (previously addressed with a\nworkaround on 2026-04-23) now has a root cause and a permanent fix.\n\n**Mechanism**: at boot, Windows' legacy `sermouse` (Serial Mouse Driver) service\nloads, and `serenum.sys` is attached as a per-device **upper filter** on\n`ACPI\\PNP0501\\SMODULEC4`. `serenum` opens COM4 exclusively to PnP-probe for a\nserial mouse. With the SBG Ellipse-D actively streaming binary into that probe\nwindow, the bus mis-handshakes and the port stays wedged below user-mode —\n`Status: OK` in PnP, but exclusive-open denied to userland. No user-mode\nprocess holds it; `handle64.exe` finds nothing.\n\n**Fix applied to mercat**:\n```powershell\nSet-Service sermouse -StartupType Disabled\n```\nMercat has no serial mouse and never will. Reverse with\n`Set-Service sermouse -StartupType Manual` if ever needed. (`Stop-Service`\nfails live because `sermouse` is a kernel driver already bound to the device\nstack — the `StartupType` change takes effect on reboot.)\n\n**Verified post-reboot**:\n- `Get-Service sermouse` → `Stopped`, `Disabled`\n- `mode COM4` → returns full port settings (previously: *\"Device COM4 is not currently available.\"*)\n- `.NET SerialPort.Open()` on COM4 @ 115200 → `IsOpen=True`, `BytesToRead=2826`\n  after 200ms — SBG actively streaming\n\n**Fallback if it ever wedges again** (e.g., a different probe culprit appears):\n```powershell\nDisable-PnpDevice -InstanceId \"ACPI\\PNP0501\\SMODULEC4\" -Confirm:$false\nEnable-PnpDevice  -InstanceId \"ACPI\\PNP0501\\SMODULEC4\" -Confirm:$false\n```\n\n**Diagnostic fingerprint** to recognize the same wedge in the future:\n- `mode COM4` → \"Device COM4 is not currently available.\"\n- COM4 in PnP shows `Status: OK` on `ACPI\\PNP0501\\SMODULEC4`\n- `handle64.exe -accepteula -a COM4` → \"No matching handles found\"\n- TeraTerm / sbgCenter / `.NET SerialPort.Open()` → \"Access to the port 'COM4' is denied.\"\n- No `Serial` / `serenum` / `sermouse` events in System log\n\n`lfsvc` (Geolocation Service) remains permanently disabled from the prior\nincident — kept as belt-and-braces, not load-bearing.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}